+# Adversarial review: open-data-pipeline_cd-1 (plan-gate, round 1)
+
+Block: P6. Plan: `.context/plans/open-data-pipeline_cd-1.plan.md` (sha256 92277bc30472c359b12c1fe17adc316791ba7d70aa75d8adbf6d0f983984ed36, cycle-5 update). Contract: `/home/user/cadence-core/skills/de-adversarial-reviewer/SKILL.md` (sha256 3846292775f8ec98794c44ceb35b3b22611c1816d019203a64d685d3dc93ec8b, same as the bench cache copy).
+
+## Verification notes
+
+- Read the whole plan (802 lines) and the peer contract, the architecture core rules, and the decision records named by the plan. The plan hash matches the Input line of the packet. The packet hash was not recomputed.
+- Input hashes in the plan match the files: spec `.context/proposals/cd-1.md` (9ae7bbd3...), vibe-test `.context/vibetest/cd-1_2026-10-21.md` (f52fef6f...). All 20 decision slugs in the plan table exist as `.context/proposals/cd-1-<slug>.md`.
+- Prior review (`.context/reviews/plan_open-data-pipeline_cd-1.md`, cycle 5, READY WITH CHANGES) left MF-8 open and added MF-10. The cycle-5 update text closes both: one in-memory dedupe set seeded from the lake (MF-8), and a bounded failure exit (MF-10). I checked the text, the named tests, and the decisions `cd-1-stream-resume` and `cd-1-stream-micro-batch`. The rules are consistent with each other. B-1 below concerns whether MF-10 may be applied at all.
+- Raw data was read in memory and never extracted (zip headers and rows; census CSVs). Counts used below:
+  - USAspending: 9,820 rows (416 contract, 9,404 assistance). All `action_date_fiscal_year` = 2024. 1,226 negative `federal_action_obligation`. No amount has more than 2 decimal places or fails to parse. 18 blank recipient county, 8 blank recipient state. 0 blank `award_id_piid`. 68 blank `award_id_fain` (assistance). 7,296 blank `award_id_uri` (assistance). 0 rows with both FAIN and URI blank.
+  - Headers: no column named `awarding_toptier_code`. The agency code column is `awarding_agency_code` (values 417, 418, 474, 485). No `generated_unique_award_id`. `contract_award_unique_key` and `assistance_award_unique_key` exist and are never blank.
+  - Census: 2024 file has 3,144 county rows (SUMLEV 050), 2021 file has 3,143. Codes 09110, 09120, 09130, 09140, 09150, 09160, 09170, 09180, 09190 are in 2024 only. Codes 09001, 09003, 09005, 09007, 09009, 09011, 09013, 09015 are in 2021 only.
