+## Trade-offs
+
+- The in-memory dedupe set, seeded from the lake, gives exactly-once without a watermark file. Its cost is memory that grows with the run, which is small for one hour of events. The cost of a restart is re-reading the open batch.
+- The planned PIID and FAIN key is readable, but the official award keys in the files are safer and already unique in this data (B-2).
+- The 2021 population fallback follows Amendment A literally. It fits poorly for Connecticut (B-3).
+- Recipient location for place is a defensible choice, and the decision records it.
+
+## Verdict
+
+The plan is not ready to execute. Three blocking items (B-1, B-2, B-3) each change a published number or a stated rule, and two of them (B-2, B-3) fail or distort a check that the plan says it will verify. The conditions can go into the next plan text.
+
+Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES
