+### C-1. The raw stream lake must hold every consumed event type, or the restart seed is wrong
+
+- Plan: Phase 4 work list (plan lines 213-224), decision `cd-1-lateness-watermark` (the seed is "the maximum event_time over the rows already landed"), and N-8 (plan lines 579-581).
+- The text does not say that `lake/stream_edit_raw/` holds events of every `type`. MF-5 filters `fct_edit` to `edit` and `new`, and the watermark counts all consumed events "of any type". If non-edit events do not land, the seed after a restart omits them, and the watermark can be lower than in an uninterrupted run. A non-edit event with a higher event time than any landed edit would then change a later `is_late`.
+- Fix: write "every consumed event of every type lands in `stream_edit_raw`" in Phase 4 and in `cd-1-lateness-watermark`. Add a restart case in `test_restart_matches_uninterrupted_run` whose fixture has a non-edit event with the highest event time before the cut.
