+### MF-1: lateness watermark counts consumed events, not landed rows
+
+Replaces the Phase 4 rule for `watermark_before`:
+
+- `watermark_before` is the running maximum of `event_time` over all events the consumer has consumed
+  before the current event, in `arrival_seq` order. It counts events that have not landed yet. The consumer
+  holds it in memory.
+- At start the consumer seeds it with the maximum `event_time` over the rows already in
+  `lake/stream_edit_raw/`. Those rows are the prefix before the resume cursor, so the seed equals the running
+  maximum that an uninterrupted run holds at that point.
+- Flush cadence (decision `stream-micro-batch`) is not an input to the rule.
+- Events consumed but not landed before a crash are consumed again after the restart, in the same order.
+  Their `is_late` is computed again with the same watermark, so the stored value is the same.
+- Decision `lateness-watermark` is updated to this rule.
+
+New Phase 4 test, `tests/test_stream_lateness.py::test_is_late_set_independent_of_flush_cadence`: the same
+replay, run with two flush cadences (every 500 events, and every 50 events), gives the same `is_late` value
+for each `meta_id`.
+
+### MF-2: arrival_seq has a restart rule
+
+- At start the counter is seeded with the maximum `arrival_seq` in the lake, plus one. If the lake holds no
+  rows, the first value is 0.
+- The counter increases strictly across a restart.
+- The watermark rule uses the arrival order only. It does not filter rows by `arrival_seq`.
+
+New Phase 4 unit test, `tests/test_stream_consumer.py::test_arrival_seq_increases_across_restart`: write
+rows with `arrival_seq` 0 to n-1, simulate a restart, and assert that the first new value is n and that
+every later value is larger.
+
+### MF-3: make build and the stream marts
+
+Behavior (a) is chosen. `make build` never runs `make stream`.
+
+- The stream models carry the dbt tag `stream`: `stg_stream_edits`, `fct_edit`, `late_events`,
+  `mart_edit_windows_5min`, and the checks `check_05_...` to `check_07_...`.
+- `make build` runs the batch ingestion (Phase 1). It then checks whether `lake/stream_edit_raw/` exists.
+  - Absent: `dbt build --exclude tag:stream`. It publishes these marts only: `fct_award_transaction`,
+    `mart_obligations_monthly`, `dim_agency`, `dim_place`, `dim_date`, `dim_wiki`.
+  - Present: the full `dbt build`. It publishes the batch marts and `fct_edit`, `late_events`,
+    `mart_edit_windows_5min`.
+- The twice-build test names the marts it compares, as listed above:
+  - `tests/test_marts_publish.py::test_clean_lake_publishes_batch_marts_only`: run on a clean `lake/` and
+    `out/`. It runs `make build` twice. The folders under `out/marts/` are exactly the batch list, and the
+    sha256 of each file is the same on both runs. This is the Phase 7 exit test.
+  - `tests/test_marts_publish.py::test_stream_lake_publishes_all_marts`: run after `make stream` has written
+    `lake/stream_edit_raw/`. It runs `make build` twice. The folders are exactly the full list, and the sha256
+    of each file is the same on both runs. This is a Phase 8 exit test.
