@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+---
+decision_id: cd-1-lateness-watermark
+status: proposed
+question: Where does the lateness watermark live across a stop and restart (G-4)?
+choice: Nowhere separate on disk. The watermark before an event is the running maximum of event_time over all events the consumer has consumed before it, in arrival order, whether or not they have landed. The consumer holds it in memory. At start it seeds the watermark with the maximum event_time over the rows already landed, which are the prefix before the resume cursor. Every consumed event of every type lands in `stream_edit_raw`, so that seed covers every event type (adversarial round 2, C-1). The is_late flag is set once, at first arrival, and stored.
+rationale: The seed comes from the landed rows, so no second stored copy can disagree with them after a crash. Counting consumed events, not landed ones, keeps the watermark independent of flush timing, so lateness follows stream time and not wall-clock time. The rejected options are a watermark file, which needs its own atomic update, and a watermark over landed rows only, which depends on when the flush runs.
+---
+Ticket: cd-1
